From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:43:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] An inventory option no longer drops your target

First of the two engine mechanisms behind "actions get cancelled for doing
anything - you should be able to do multiple things" and "pvp is way off,
everything feels delayed", reported from play 2026-09-21. Deliberately alone,
so what it changes can be felt on its own.

OpHeldHandler called clearPendingAction(), which is closeModal() PLUS
clearInteraction(), and clearInteraction() sets this.target = null. The
player's attack loop is driven by that target, so eating, drinking, burying or
equipping anything stopped you attacking. It now calls closeModal() alone: the
dialogue still goes away, the fight does not.

Upstream LostCityRS is identical here - I cloned it and diffed - so this is a
divergence rather than a fix, decided by Corey: Old School feel over 2004
authenticity.

NOT TOUCHED: the `if (player.delayed) return false` at the top of this file and
its fifteen siblings, which DISCARDS a click made during a delay instead of
deferring it. That is the second mechanism and it is a bigger change; it wants
its own branch and its own session in game. OpHeldU and OpHeldT keep the clear,
because using one item on another is its own action rather than something you
do mid-fight.

NOT COMPILED OR RUN. npm has been 403ing zod for days, so nothing in the cloud
can build this engine; tsc will not even load its node types here. The change
is a one-line swap to a method already called in three other places in
Player.ts, and the first real test is Corey building and playing it.

Analysis: Content/claude/combat-delays-investigation.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dc7giZ7Qnh4qy1CYPTDrmH
